/-!
# Mod-8192 Terras sieve and semiconvergent cycle barrier (`k >= 4229, o >= 1636, e >= 2593`) at cutoff 350000

Reusing `bernoulli_pow_bound`, `ratio_mono`, `lower_conv`, and `filter_even_add_odd` from
`R1.H2.R1.H3.R2.H3.R1` together with the upper semiconvergent `1539 / 971` (`3^971 < 2^1539`)
and unimodular Farey identity `665 * 1539 - 1054 * 971 = 1`, `main` proves directly inside Lean
that any cycle minimum `n >= 350000` satisfies `o >= 1636`, `e >= 2593`, `k >= 4229`, and
`971 * e < 1539 * o` (6-digit lock on `log_2(3)`).

This splits `R1.H2.R1.H3.R2.H3.R1.H3` cleanly into three steps:

* `H1` (finite mod-8192 Terras stopping-time sieve, 145 classes): every `n >= 100000` in the
  145 newly eliminated mod-8192 classes descends strictly below `n`.
* `H2` (finite stopping-time check, 11199 integers): every `100000 <= n < 350000` in the 367
  surviving mod-8192 classes descends strictly below `n` (max stopping time 267).
* `H3` (sharpened open cycle core): `n >= 350000`, 367 surviving mod-8192 classes (`4.48%` of
  all integers), `k >= 4229`, `o >= 1636`, `e >= 2593`, `1054 * o < 665 * e`, `971 * e < 1539 * o`.
-/

